  "label": "homestead credit",
  "note": "Arkansas taxes a home on 20% of its market value. Every homestead gets up to a $600 credit off the bill (Amendment 79); the state repays the local governments for it, so they still receive the full amount shown below.",
  "limits": "The $600 homestead credit is applied in full when the bill is large enough; Amendment 79 also limits how fast a homestead’s assessed value can rise, which isn’t modeled."
 },
